From c8d39e171b3753e8a15ddbc27048c0a1bad54379 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 13:55:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Finance stabilization: payment form crash, filter label,
 tournament costs

ST-005 -- Payment editing
  PaymentForm referenced its own player-eligibility list (available) about
  40 lines before declaring it. Any edit path that rendered this form --
  Add payment, Edit payment/obligation, Edit Total Due, Edit Team Dues --
  hit a ReferenceError from the temporal dead zone. The two declarations
  now run first; nothing about which players are eligible changed.
  Total Due can be lowered, but never below what is already legitimately
  recorded as paid. Enforced server-side in savePlayerPayment, not just in
  the form: an attempt below that floor is rejected before any write, with
  a message naming the amount already paid. Existing payment history is
  never touched by a Total Due edit -- only the obligation changes. The
  bulk Team Dues protection added earlier is unchanged.

ST-006 -- Finance filter label
  The payment-status filter labeled "Paid" while its badges read "Paid in
  full" elsewhere on the same screen. Label changed to match; the filter
  still selects the same players it always did.

ST-007 -- Tournament costs and budget-line integrity
  total_cost is a generated column computed from entry_fee + gate_fee. A
  tournament with one fee set and the other left blank generated NULL
  instead of the fee that was actually entered, so that cost silently
  never reached Finance. Blank fee fields are now written as 0 rather than
  left null, so the generated total reflects what was actually entered.
  Every other place total_cost is read (Finance, the tournament list, the
  drawer) already treated a blank fee as 0 for display -- this closes the
  one path, the write, that did not.

  Separately: a budget line referenced by a tournament could be deleted
  with no warning whenever that tournament had no transaction filed yet --
  the normal state for a Committed event nobody has paid toward -- silently
  clearing the tournament's allocation. Budget line deletion now checks for
  linked tournaments the same way it already checks for linked transactions:
  blocked, named, with a "Review tournament" link that opens the tournament
  directly on its Costs section so the coach can change or clear the
  allocation before returning to delete the line. The database foreign key
  backing this (tournaments.budget_item_id) changes from ON DELETE SET NULL
  to ON DELETE RESTRICT to match the same protection already in place on
  budget_transactions, as a backstop for any write path that bypasses the
  app.
